From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elias Bakken <elias@iagent.no>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 20:22:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] recore: load BL31 into DRAM to make room for Klipper

A64's BL31 sits at 0x00044000 by default, in the middle of the low memory
Klipper wants. We build TF-A with SUNXI_BL31_IN_DRAM=1 so it links at
0x40000000, and u-boot has to load it there to match.

Up to v2024.01 that meant patching a #define BL31_ADDR into
arch/arm/dts/sunxi-u-boot.dtsi. From v2026.07 the address is a Kconfig
symbol instead - arch/arm/mach-sunxi/Kconfig:

    config SUNXI_BL31_BASE
            default 0x00044000 if MACH_SUN50I || MACH_SUN50I_H5
            default 0x40000000 if MACH_SUN50I_H616

and sunxi-u-boot.dtsi uses it for the FIT entry:

    load  = <CONFIG_SUNXI_BL31_BASE>;
    entry = <CONFIG_SUNXI_BL31_BASE>;

so this is now one defconfig line rather than a source patch.

Signed-off-by: Elias Bakken <elias@iagent.no>
---
 configs/recore_defconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/configs/recore_defconfig
+++ b/configs/recore_defconfig
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
 CONFIG_ARM=y
+CONFIG_SUNXI_BL31_BASE=0x40000000
 CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI=y
 CONFIG_SPL=y
